            <ArticleTitle>[New contributions on extinction tests of essential headache. III. The test with tiapride].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1139-41</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The Authors valued effects of the extinction-test with Thiapride (200 mg i.v.) in the primary headaches. They particularly noticed a significant reduction of PGF2-alpha and PRL, together with an increase of 5-HT and beta-ELI in CSF.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
